A simple L-System plotter

UI UPDATE!!!!

Made for hackClub terra 26/27

### How to use:

Click and drag to explore the plot.
Hit space to reset the view.
Zoom using your mouse wheel.

### Explanation

This project consists of an L-System calculator and a graphics turtle.

An L-System takes a set of rules and applies them to a an axiom (starting string).
This results in a state like this:

Axiom: A
Rules:
-> A => AB
-> B => A

0: A
1: AB
2: ABA
3: ABAAB

The turtle will take the current state
and use rules to plot it out on the screen:

A => Forward
B => Turn left 20°

This results in some really funky and organic looking structures.
These L-Systems get very large, very quickly (usually double their size about every iteration)
so be mindful of that when plotting past 15 iterations.

